From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 014/NNN] build: give the selected mbedtls priority over any other

Every consumer of SEC_INCLUDE_DIRS adds it after the include paths
inherited from the top level. When a second mbedtls sits in one of those,
for example a newer one in a Homebrew prefix, its headers are used with the
selected version's library.

That combination does not compile. mbedtls 4 moved mbedtls_md_hmac behind
MBEDTLS_DECLARE_PRIVATE_IDENTIFIERS, so srsran/common/ssl.h fails against
its header even when the 3.x library being linked exports the symbol.

BEFORE puts the chosen include directory first.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-09-03 15:18:08
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-09-03 15:18:08
@@ -185,6 +185,14 @@
 find_package(MbedTLS REQUIRED)
 if (MBEDTLS_FOUND)
   set(SEC_INCLUDE_DIRS "${MBEDTLS_INCLUDE_DIRS}")
+  # BEFORE matters when more than one mbedtls is installed. Every consumer of
+  # SEC_INCLUDE_DIRS adds it after the include paths inherited from here, so a
+  # second copy of mbedtls sitting in one of those, for example a newer one in
+  # a Homebrew prefix, supplies the headers instead. That mixes headers from
+  # one version with the library of another: mbedtls 4 hides mbedtls_md_hmac
+  # behind MBEDTLS_DECLARE_PRIVATE_IDENTIFIERS, so srsran/common/ssl.h fails to
+  # compile even though the 3.x library being linked exports it.
+  include_directories(BEFORE ${MBEDTLS_INCLUDE_DIRS})
   if(BUILD_STATIC)
     set(SEC_LIBRARIES    "${MBEDTLS_STATIC_LIBRARIES}")
   else(BUILD_STATIC)
